❌️ So, to sum up? There is nothing "sunny" about @sunny Hostin's double standards and political resentment; and people can see through it.

📣 Hence, viewers are way better off letting the sun finally set on her hateful media career.

@elonmusk
@RealCandaceO
@megynkelly
@joerogan
@TuckerCarlson

@washingtonpost So much for the hyped..wait reduction
-
The U.S. Food and Drug Administration, after intense public pressure and a lawsuit, is reconsidering its declaration barely 2 weeks ago that a shortage of the appetite-suppressing drugs Mounjaro &amp; Zepbound is over. https://t.co/Jenk4kFHBt

@AllisonPearson Side-effects For tirzepatide
Common or very common
Alopecia; appetite decreased  (in patients with type 2 diabetes); asthenia; burping; constipation;  diarrhoea; dizziness; gastrointestinal discomfort; gastrointestinal  disorders; hypersensitivity; hypotension; lethargy; malaise;

@Paul_Reviews Hi Paul.  I didn't start losing until 7.5mg mounjaro and I know an awful lot of people are the same. I'm now on 10mg and it's my "sweetspot" dose
I'm averaging 2 to 3 lbs a week now.   I was around 2 stone (28lbs) overweight and that's gone now.
Good luck

@Rrrrnessa There are a number of support groups on Facebook and Reddit, some of which are post mounjaro.
It's not a straightforward answer, if you over indulge after any prolonged diet the same thing happens.
It's a complex medicine that does more than just suppress appetite.

@VPrasadMDMPH The GLP-1 meds produces incredibly rapid weight loss

I took compounded tirzepatide at full strength for only 2 weeks—to maintain a weight loss, not to lose further—&amp; instantly dropped 4 pounds

If you’ve had the experience of losing appetite, you know how fast fat disappears

@Tjeerd001 C. 
I was on Ozempic for 18 months (diabetes 2) now on Mounjaro for 
7 weeks. I haven't lost an ounce.  But my A1C numbers are good, which is the actual point.

@Gadea It's more effective for weight-loss.
Mounjaro is a GLP-1 and GIP receptor agonist. Ozempic acts only on GLP-1.
Nearly 82% of Mounjaro patients lost at least 5% of their body weight, compared with 67% of patients who took Ozempic.

@AllisonPearson @AllisonPearson 

A yr ago I was prescribed with 'Rybelsus' (appetite suppression tablet). This combined with walking 50km a week has resulted in 4.5 stone loss

NHS doctor so impressed with my commitment, she has now prescribed the Mounjaro jab to help me lose 3 more stones

@f1lechair @Ruesavatar I'm on Mounjaro as well and for me the biggest factor is feeling full after a smaller portion. 

It's amazing and I've lost forty pounds so far and it's helped in so many ways; better sleep, less back pain, more mobility. 

I'm extremely grateful GLP1 drugs exist

@EliLillyandCo released topline Phase III data on Monday showing that after more than three years of follow-up, pre-diabetic patients treated with tirzepatide were less likely to progress to type 2 diabetes.

https://t.co/b3KSvAOexz

#pharma #diabetes #biospace
